<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian stocks seen firmer on offshore finishes.</title>
<headline>Australian stocks seen firmer on offshore finishes.</headline>
<text>
<p>-----------------(Snapshot 8.30 a.m./2230 GMT)-----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	   2699.10   +4.70   DJIA  cl	7921.82  +35.06</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl	 2713	+4   US 30yr cl	 6.53   -0.03</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    93.340  +0.030   Gold NY 321.30 Lon fix 319.50</p>
<p>AUD	   0.7397 (Fri 0.7445)   CRB Index cl   233.52   +0.82</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	19875.49 +120.71   FTSE cl	 4799.50  +31.70</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   924.50   +0.10   NZSE40	  2509.82   -7.02</p>
<p>--------------------------(July 14)----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks seen up on offshore strength, rate cut hopes still alive. &quot;The U.S. was quite strong and metals were a little better but there won't be a rate cut just yet,&quot; said one broker.  </p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$18.75 (steady), A$19.90 (-.05), A$6.42 (-.01), A$7.79 (-.005)</p>
<p>*Wall Street stocks staged a broad rally that was paced by stirring gains in the computer group.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 19 (-5/16), BHP 28-1/8 (+1/4), WMC 23-11/16 (+3/8), National Australia Bank 74-1/16 (+1/4)</p>
<p>*Gold ended higher on fund short-covering, while base metals prices also skipped higher, boosted by end of week covering.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
